 - daily puzzle
 - shared leaderboard (would require actual server infrastructure)
 - logos with friends: collaborative puzzle
   - less awful lobby / invite infrastructure; this will require an
     actual server under our control, even if it is only doing the
     rendezvous. Probably worth it as the current system is super
     awkward.
   - more symmetric view of the players; only the host talks to each
     player, so guest 1 doesn't even know about guest 2
   - show multiplayer info all the time while connected; probably this
     should replace the logo during online play (with perhaps a smaller
     logo retained). Probably the primary view should be a list of
     players.
   - cursor sharing (again, this probably wants a direct connection
     between players, but we should be able to facilitate the webrtc
     setup once via the host). Each player gets their own color-tinted
     stylus (or perhaps we can reintroduce the gear).
   - maybe: attribute moves to players. This might be hard to do in a
     way that is not visually distracting, though (and with cursor
     sharing you can kind of see it in real-time anyway)
 - consider simplifying
   - are chalk marks worth the interface complexity
   - is drag tiles any good
   - is release-to-act a good feature
 - evaluate clue interactions
   - is rearranging / dragging clues useful?
   - is highlighting clues that refer to a symbol useful?
   - what UI should expose highlighting? Current experiments use
     shift-click on a clue and pressing a filled board slot.
 - wire up difficulty levels
   - puzzleDifficulty(puzzle) now returns a score and easy/medium/hard
     label; see DIFFICULTY.md for the scoring model and play tests
   - rate generated candidates and retry until one matches the requested
     difficulty; keep seed meanings stable, and play explicitly requested
     seeds regardless of the difficulty preference
   - add difficulty selection to the Game section in Options; probably
     checkboxes so players can choose one level or a mix
   - show the current puzzle's difficulty
   - pantheon should mark difficulty and/or keep separate pantheon
     for various levels
 - run history
   - we're now storing all runs via indexdb
   - run history should be exportable (maybe even just using dev tools)
     to feed difficulty analysis (e.g., seeing what is really "hard"
     based on completion times).
   - add filtering by difficulty, date range, and elapsed-time range
